<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia raises Dec palm olein export tax.</title>
<headline>Indonesia raises Dec palm olein export tax.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia raised its export tax on RBD palm olein to $41.30/tonne in December from $18.75 in November, the Finance Ministry said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tax on crude palm oil was raised to $44.72/tonne from $28.00 in November, the ministry said in a statement.  </p>
<p>The tax on RBD palm oil was raised to $33.04/tonne in December from $19.20, while that on crude olein was raised to $44.80/tonne from $22.50 in November.</p>
<p>The taxes, introduced in September 1994, are based on the composite average of international prices in the last two weeks of the previous month and are aimed at ensuring sufficient supply and price stability in the local market.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom + 6221 384-6364</p>
</text>
